id: pm-evidence-portable-bundles
title: Transfer selected retained citations as validated portable bundles
description: "Export selected evidence artifacts with exact hashes, source descriptors, explicit sharing consent and omission policy. Validate complete bundles and explicit revision-bound target authorization before inspecting or importing."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: backlog-1021,portable-bundles
created_at: "2026-10-28T20:14:00.476Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T18:04:32.491Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-30T18:04:30.628Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-29T00:27:37.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Tampered bytes refuse before writes; export excludes unselected sources; a no-git recipient replays retained fragments without original files; revoked consent prevents new export; 500 seeded model sequences compare native SDK read-back; packed npm and Bun acceptance; unchanged full release thresholds
release: 2026.10.30
resolution: "Delivered by PR #17 (eec7dc8): Replay selected retained citations from portable bundles"
expected_result: Tampered bytes refuse before writes; export excludes unselected sources; a no-git recipient replays retained fragments without original files; revoked consent prevents new export; 500 seeded model sequences compare native SDK read-back; packed npm and Bun acceptance; unchanged full release thresholds
actual_result: "PR #17 merged at 2026-10-29T00:27:37Z as eec7dc8; required CI passed on the merged head."
comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T20:14:06.625Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: installed CLI SDK declarations expose native history replay, output receipts, fenced mutateItem, complete reads and artifact deduplication, but no retained citation transport. Existing pm-evidence replay requires a citation already on an item; pm-memory import/export transfers knowledge records and guidance, while context/review/rlm consume evidence. This feature transports explicitly selected evidence fragments and source identity on existing native items; no tracker creation or generic archive. Reuse citationSchema, replay, Store and SDK fenced mutation; preserve native relationships and unrelated fields. No pm-evidence entry exists in the older no-git audit, so direct non-git acceptance is required."
  "2026-10-28T20:27:16.862Z",codex-agent,"Implemented explicit sharing grant/revoke, bounded hash-verified retained artifact bundles, compact CLI receipts and SDK inspect/import APIs. All transfer authorization and unchanged decisions read current native state under SDK fenced leases, using verified native history generation to reject ABA and stale retries; preview and apply share one planner. Target foreign evidence is preserved with a typed skip. Focused bundle and command tests pass; new bundle modules measured 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines in the focused coverage run. Public snapshot at 2224762: 15 items, 37 read-only files verified unchanged, 6 cited artifacts, 5 explicitly exported, 1 excluded, 3964 bundle bytes, 360 retained bytes, 5 source-free SDK replays, zero retry additions, tamper refusal and revoked export refusal; metadata inspection 502 estimated tokens."
  "2026-10-28T20:35:01.314Z",codex-agent,"Validation: 9 focused bundle/CLI/concurrency tests pass, including the pm test --run --only-index 1 --progress journey (result tracking is disabled by project policy; result recorded here). Seed 0xb0d1e2026 passed 500 sequences / 2000 operations / 2000 SDK target read-backs on 25 trackers: 109 imports, 555 unchanged replays, 67 sharing refusals and 512 validated producer bundles. Native parent/dependency edges, custom active/blocked statuses and ambient focus were exercised. Five isolated function-only negative controls each failed exactly one behavioral test: checksum, explicit selection, native generation authorization, live sharing consent and retained bytes; restored disposable implementation passed 4/4. Typecheck, lint, zero-duplication and docstring gates pass. No local full release suite was launched; full npm/Bun evidence will come from exact-head CI."
  "2026-10-28T20:36:55.856Z",codex-agent,"Overlap additionally verified against the installed current 2026.10.28 CLI SDK declarations: native history/evidence reads exist, no retained-citation transport API. Local health reports only extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew from an inherited newer pm-github extension outside this package; settings, storage, integrity and history drift checks pass. No global configuration or telemetry changes were made. CI uses the pinned host on a clean runner and remains the authoritative full health/release gate. Filesystem no-git support is verified; remote atomic mutation conformance remains explicitly outside the existing backend-conformance item scope."
  "2026-10-28T20:37:52.731Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance passes 2/2 journeys: npm/npx and Bun/bunx, project-local executables, embedded SDK and both global pm installs all exercise bundle transport and unchanged retry. Remote atomic mutation conformance is outside this feature and remains tracked by pm-evidence-backend-conformance; no new SDK gap was encountered. The ready review PR will use CI npm release gates on Node 22 and 26 plus the Bun gate on Node 26 at unchanged 100/100/100/100 coverage and zero duplication thresholds. All later gate results will be linked in the PR, preserving final-head tracker history."
  "2026-10-28T20:44:40.271Z",codex-agent,"Final review follow-through: add a persisted retained citation fixture produced by the released baseline, extend sharing/consent boundary interleavings, and verify that CLI file reads consume one complete unchanged bounded snapshot before parsing. These strengthen the compatibility and complete-input acceptance contracts while CI remains queued."
  "2026-10-28T20:50:39.627Z",codex-agent,"Follow-through verified: 12/12 focused tests pass; both new bundle modules remain measured at 100/100/100/100 in focused coverage. Six isolated function-only controls each fail exactly one test (including complete CLI input snapshot); restored implementation passes 5/5 bundle tests. Added exact native evidence state emitted by the released v2026.10.28 producer with synthetic CRLF source: it reads/replays unchanged, refuses unconsented export, and exports after a grant. Eight import plus eight sharing/consent interleavings and an actual held-lease competing writer pass. CLI rejects incomplete reads and same-size file edits before parsing. Final model assertions now also compare complete origin/provenance, normalized SDK artifact links, native comment text/author and review attribution. CI run 40765210411 on initial head remains queued; final follow-up head requires fresh exact-head CI. The original 30-minute CI waiting cutoff remains in effect."
  "2026-10-28T21:09:23.213Z",codex-agent,"CI waiting cutoff: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/actions/runs/40767010453 for source head 74b00898573ff7d7f98f1675a43d5051bb9124ad remains pending after the required 30-minute total waiting window. Node 26 tracker health and identity/privacy passed; its full npm release gate is running, Node 22 is queued, and the Bun release gate has not started. Completed full release gates: 0 of 3; no full-suite pass count is claimed. Initial run 40765210411 was superseded/canceled and is excluded from evidence. Final review also fixed aggregate allocation bounds before JSON serialization in both export and validation, with raw/escaped oversize refusals; bundle tests pass 5/5 and bundles.ts remains 100/100/100/100. The final commit requires fresh exact-head CI; pending results are for orchestrator follow-through, not approval."
  "2026-10-28T21:10:54.634Z",codex-agent,"Final local results: all seven isolated behavioral negative controls fail exactly one test, including aggregate transport bounds; restored implementation passes 5/5 bundle tests. Latest-code public-data replay again verifies the same 15 items, 37 unchanged files, 5 of 6 artifacts, 3964 bundle bytes, 360 retained bytes, 5 exact replays, zero retry additions and 502-token inspection. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, 126 documented declarations, identity and changelog checks pass. CI waiting ended at the mandated cutoff; latest-head npm/Bun full release counts remain pending. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item remains open for closure by the orchestrator."
  "2026-10-28T22:03:58.400Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: the blocking finding violates additive ownership: evidence source discovery may add absent native file links but must preserve every existing path/scope annotation, including empty or absent notes. Package-wide search found a single writer projection in src/store.ts shared by import, consent, cite, check, review and criterion binding; all CLI and SDK mutation paths converge there. The model oracle also used incoming-favoring deduplication and lacked colliding native fixtures, so it must be strengthened without dropping existing assertions. Git status was clean and origin/main is already an ancestor (3 commits ahead, 0 behind), so no merge is needed. GitHub contains no actionable non-blocking review findings beyond the supplied orchestrator finding; all supplied findings will be addressed."
  "2026-10-28T22:16:16.955Z",codex-agent,"Class fix and focused evidence: writeEvidence now uses SDK artifactKey on the current leased native file list, filters out already-owned identities before deduplication, and declares a files change only for actual additions. This covers all package mutation commands through their one shared projection. SDK ownership test passes 30 operation/note-domain combinations; peer annotations survive all eight CAS boundaries; CLI import/check and native JSON/TOON rendering pass in non-git trackers. The renderer test captures each native presentation before and after rather than hand-normalizing undefined versus null. The 500-sequence model now seeds colliding project/global identities, missing notes and native annotation revisions, comparing against an independent first-owner map. Packed local/global npm/Bun journeys seed source and recipient annotations. Behavioral revert in a disposable source copy replaces only writeEvidence with the pre-fix function: fail 1 with Native annotation changed; restoring the fixed function passes 1 across all 30 combinations. No existing tests or thresholds were weakened."
  "2026-10-28T22:30:35.022Z",codex-agent,"Full-gate diagnostic: the first npm run exposed a model-only ordering assumption and was stopped rather than consuming the host on a known failure. The oracle had sorted baseline native links before any evidence write, whereas the SDK native write preserves their insertion order. The independent reference now retains observed native ordering until a genuinely new file identity invokes SDK sorting. Added an exact native-array order assertion for imports with no absent identities. Annotation ownership assertions remain intact; no production behavior or test threshold was relaxed."
  "2026-10-28T22:43:36.894Z",codex-agent,"Oracle refinement: SDK dedupeLinkedArtifacts preserves insertion order; sorting is a separate SDK operation and is not part of native evidence publication. The model now keeps a first-owner insertion-ordered map, observes native annotation edits through the SDK, and adds only missing cited identities on any target evidence mutation. This corrects the earlier sorting assumption in the diagnostic comment. The full model is being run standalone to completion before restarting either full release gate; production remains the same SDK-key ownership fix."
  "2026-10-28T23:12:57.684Z",codex-agent,"Focused model completion: seed 0xb0d1e2026 passes all 500 sequences / 2000 operations / 2000 SDK target read-backs across 25 trackers with colliding native artifact identities and native note edits. Results: 109 imports, 555 unchanged replays, 67 consent refusals, 512 validated producer bundles. Exact native annotations, absent notes, project/global identities and insertion order remain intact. Two earlier local full-suite attempts were stopped after model-oracle ordering failures; those attempts are not approval evidence. The corrected standalone model is fully green. Per the original saturated-host instruction, full npm and Bun release gates will be executed by fresh exact-head CI, with the existing two-worker suite configuration and unchanged coverage/duplication thresholds. No additional non-blocking findings were supplied or found in GitHub review comments; the supplied additive-ownership class is addressed in every shared writer path."
  "2026-10-28T23:38:24.666Z",codex-agent,"Compatibility completion of the same additive-ownership class: the public SDK canonical document and mutation APIs accept legacy file collections containing multiple rows with the same path/scope and distinct annotations. Deduplicating the entire native collection when adding a new source can discard such a foreign row. The writer now leaves the complete existing native list untouched and deduplicates only package-owned additions. Added a real-SDK legacy duplicate fixture covering both CAS check recording and locked bundle import. The 9aed762 CI run passed npm on Node 22 and the Node 26 npm step; Bun is still running. These results are prior-head evidence and do not approve the final compatibility completion. The original post-push waiting cutoff is retained."
  "2026-10-28T23:43:25.627Z",codex-agent,"Final class proof: SDK check recording and locked import preserve every row of a valid legacy duplicate native-file collection while appending missing identities. Two function-only negative controls run in a disposable copy: pre-fix 0e6614a fails the 30-combination native-annotation matrix; partial 9aed762 fails the legacy-duplicate preservation test. Restoring the final writer passes each focused regression (two negative failures and two restored passes). Updated npm/npx and Bun/bunx packed journeys passed 2/2 on 9aed762, including first global imports and source/recipient annotations; final compatibility change preserves their unique-identity behavior and requires fresh exact-head CI. Current run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/actions/runs/40785975485 passed npm Node 22 and the Node 26 npm step; Bun remains running as of this receipt. These are prior-head results, not final approval. The final head needs fresh full gates, and the post-push cutoff is still 23:45 UTC (30 minutes from this review-cycle push). All known supplied findings are addressed; no SDK defect or new gap was found."
